{"kind":"request","text":"codex: joining presence and chat should ask the person their name and show that, not a hash. Hugh asked for this and it is small, independent of the playability design, and can land first.\n\nWHAT HAPPENS NOW. app.js renders participants as participant.actor.slice(0, 12) and chat lines as message.actor.slice(0, 10). So a person joining sees themselves and everyone else as a truncated fingerprint. Nobody is asked for a name and there is nowhere to put one.\n\nWHY THIS NEEDS NO DURABLE RECORD. Presence and chat are already leased and ephemeral — the code says motion hints live only in leased presence and disappear on renewal, revocation or expiry. A display name for those channels belongs in the same place: carried in the presence payload, expiring with the lease. chess/name@0 exists but is the creator-only act that names a game, not an actor, so it is the wrong tool here and should not be stretched to fit.\n\nTHE ONE THING I WANT CAREFUL. A self-asserted name in an ephemeral channel is spoofable by construction: anyone may claim to be anyone. That is acceptable for a chat label and unacceptable anywhere authority is shown. So the name must never replace a verifiable identity where a seat, a move or a durable act is attributed — it may sit beside one, but the thing a reader relies on to know who moved must stay the thing the signature proves. Getting this wrong would make the UI lie about identity, which is worse than showing a hash.\n\nThe rest is ordinary: bound the length, keep markup and control characters off the page, refuse an empty name, and fall back to today's truncated fingerprint when nobody supplies one so that an agent joining without a name is unaffected.","body":{"conditions":"Independent of the playability design 967e62b6 and landable before it. Joining presence and chat prompts for a display name and carries it in the leased presence payload alongside the existing public key, so it expires with the lease exactly as motion hints do. No durable record is created and the fold is not touched. The participant list and chat lines show the display name where one is given, and fall back to the current truncated fingerprint where none is. The name is bounded in length, refused or escaped so that no markup or control characters reach the page, and refused if it is empty or whitespace only. It must not be presented as identity where authority is at stake: wherever a seat, a move, or a durable act is attributed, the verifiable actor identity remains visible and the self-asserted name may accompany it but never replaces it. A regression test asserts a supplied name renders, a missing name falls back to the fingerprint, and a name carrying markup does not reach the page as markup; each assertion written from the desired behaviour. Embedded bundle rebuilt so the served UI matches the source. gofmt, build, vet and the full suite green at the exact head with -count=1; exact clean pushed head with per-path artifacts; independent review before merge. Write no initiative or type tags; proposal 5409bc64 is unratified.","severity":"normal","to":"09c97907402e7747d051c0c599d9eb463c48d19825820a3e4c433cde2e60e2a8"}}